# debug information files
*.dwo

# Build artifacts — generated by `make`, never commit these.
# kernel.iso embeds a wall-clock creation timestamp, so it changes on every
# build and, being binary, cannot be merged. isodir/ is scratch space that
# both `make clean` and `make kernel.iso` wipe with `rm -rf`; its grub.cfg is
# copied from the repo root each build, so tracking it only caused `make
# clean` to show up as a deleted tracked file.
*.iso
isodir/
